--- Previous Run Attempts (SRAM macro integration) ---
5 prior runs attempted full bnn_top P&R with sky130_sram_*_1rw1r macros.
All failed at GlobalRouting (GRT-0118) due to full-body met1+met2 obstructions
in the OpenRAM macros creating ~11,000 routing blockages that prevent standard
cell signal routing regardless of die size or macro arrangement.
Root cause: 8 macros in parallel (required for 256-bit word width) span 3200 µm
of die width; met1/met2 obstructions block the primary routing layers across
the entire SRAM row. Documented in synthesis_notes.md.
